AINewsDaily is a single-module Android app (Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, Hilt, Retrofit/Moshi/OkHttp, Coil, Timber) that loads US top headlines from News API (v2/top-headlines with country=us, pageSize=20, page, sortBy=publishedAt). The articles feature spans ArticleApi, NetworkModule, ArticlesResponseDto/ArticleDto, ArticleRepository, ArticleViewModel, ArticleUiState/ArticleUiEvent, and ArticleScreen. MainActivity is @AndroidEntryPoint and hosts ArticleScreen. AINewsDailyApplication is @HiltAndroidApp and plants a debug Timber tree. The UI shows “Top Stories”, a featured first item (full-width image, title, description, date) and compact items after that, with loading/error states, network retry (strings.xml), pull-to-refresh, end-of-list loading via loadNextPage(), and a bottom loader when isLoadingMore is true. NEWS_API_KEY is injected via BuildConfig from local.properties (app/build.gradle.kts); gradle.properties no longer defines it.

Files touched in this work (present in repo): ArticleApi.kt, ArticleRepository.kt, ArticlesResponseDto.kt, ArticleViewModel.kt, ArticleUiState.kt, ArticleUiEvent.kt, ArticleScreen.kt, ArticleData.kt, NetworkError.kt, ArticleDateFormatter.kt, MainActivity.kt, AINewsDailyApplication.kt, AndroidManifest.xml, strings.xml, app/build.gradle.kts, gradle/libs.versions.toml. ArticleUiModel / ArticleUiMapper are not in the repo. Dates are formatted in ArticleDto.toArticleData() using formatArticleDate(); the UI displays article.date as-is. Refresh-failure snackbar text is hardcoded in ArticleViewModel ("Network refresh failed", "Something went wrong during refresh"), not in strings.xml. Pagination uses hasMorePages = nextArticles.isNotEmpty() (and the same on first load), not “stop when articles.size < pageSize” as discussed. An earlier ./gradlew assembleDebug succeeded; a later sandbox run failed with “Unable to locate a Java Runtime”; the pagination-session build/lint runs were interrupted and did not finish in chat.

Current behavior and pitfalls for the next developer: ArticleViewModel keeps currentPage, hasMorePages, and a shared fetchJob for initial load, refresh, and pagination; pagination errors log via Timber and clear isLoadingMore without a user-visible error. ArticleScreen triggers onLoadMore when the last visible index is within 2 of the end (snapshotFlow + LaunchedEffect(listState)), without filtering on isLoadingMore in that flow. ArticleData lives under presentation.model but is used by the data layer. Empty list shows hardcoded "No articles available" (not in strings.xml). Build with ./gradlew assembleDebug; set NEWS_API_KEY in local.properties. Do not assume ArticleUiModel/mapper exist; do not assume pagination stops on partial page size until that logic is changed in ArticleViewModel.

We have created a NetworkModule file under core/di/ package that is going to provide all the dependencies like the ArticleApi, SourcesApi and any other APIs that we might add in the future.
